w: Rose tri- um- phant Eas- ter mor- ning, At the ear- ly pur- ple daw- ning.
w: None can ful- ly sing the glo- ry Of the re- sur- rec- tion sto- ry.
w: Yet didst break all bands a- sun- der, Must I not re- joice and won- der? 
w: Though the dark grave yawn be- fore me, Yet the light of hope shines o'er me.
w: Death it- self is tran- si- to- ry, I shall lift my head in glo- ry. 
